UTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible on c6c4c55146fa4da4a2b7166b51c9eb33180c5c9b (master).\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.5.beta.mono (my fork, but it's irrelevant - see description) - macOS Sequoia (15.5.0) - Multi-window, 1 monitor - Metal (Forward+) - integrated Apple M3 Pro (Apple9) - Apple M3 Pro (11 threads) - 18.00 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/108858 makes the `DisplayServer` return `FEATURE_MOUSE` as supported when running in an embedded game view on macOS.\n\nThis changes how `Viewport.get_mouse_position()` calculates its value...\n\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/de463e0241b0b846fdd3ff76ad12fe6fcf62a9e5/scene/main/viewport.cpp#L1455-L1462\n\n... resulting in an incorrect value being returned.\n\nIn my case - using a 4K monitor set to 2560x1440 resolution, it returns:\n- (0, 0) when mouse is at the bottom left of the screen\n- (5120, -2880) (negative Y) when mouse is at the top right of the screen\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1.\n```csharp\nGD.Print(GetViewport().GetMousePosition());\n```\n2. Start game in embedded game view\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nN/A","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/R